   "sols": [
    [
     [
      "Squares that share an edge in the net become faces that meet along an edge of the cube, so they can never be opposite.",
      "check pairs that are further apart"
     ],
     [
      "Fold the net keeping square <i>A</i> flat as the top of the cube: <i>B</i> folds down to become the right-hand face and <i>C</i> folds round to become the front face.",
      "each square turns through 90\u00b0 along the shared edge"
     ],
     [
      "<i>D</i> is joined to <i>C</i> and folds underneath, so the face opposite <i>A</i> is <b><i>D</i></b>",
      "top and bottom"
     ]
    ],
    [
     [
      "Continuing the fold, <i>E</i> is joined to <i>D</i> and becomes the left-hand face of the cube.",
      ""
     ],
     [
      "<i>B</i> is the right-hand face, so the face opposite <i>B</i> is <b><i>E</i></b>",
      "left and right"
     ]
    ],
    [
     [
      "Finally <i>F</i> is joined to <i>E</i> and becomes the back face.",
      ""
     ],
     [
      "<i>C</i> is the front face, so the face opposite <i>C</i> is <b><i>F</i></b>",
      "front and back"
     ],
     [
      "Check: the three pairs <i>A</i>\u2013<i>D</i>, <i>B</i>\u2013<i>E</i> and <i>C</i>\u2013<i>F</i> use all six faces exactly once \u2713",
      ""
     ]
    ]
   ]
